From d219068742503426c2e7ceeadbb2b59dd9f7d000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thampan <joby.thampan@intel.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2020 18:32:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] DRV_DPM_SW-334: Pce rule index management for CTP and Global
 region

    - Common Framework to add PCE rules, Index will be managed by the framework
    - Using Sub-Block FirstIndex can change where to start sub-block entries,
    - Using Sub-block protected flag can protect the sub-block from deleting
    - All entries in will be displayed in cat /sys/kernel/debug/dp/pce
    - Debugging can be done by enabling/disabling pce debug echo enable/disable pce > dp/dbg
    - Block delete is added to delete all rules in the sub-block @ once
---
 drivers/net/datapath/dpm/Makefile        |    2 +-
 drivers/net/datapath/dpm/datapath.h      |    9 +-
 drivers/net/datapath/dpm/datapath_api.c  |    5 +
 drivers/net/datapath/dpm/datapath_pce.c  | 1434 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/net/datapath/dpm/datapath_proc.c |    5 +-
 include/net/datapath_api.h               |   79 ++
 6 files changed, 1531 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

